# Dependencies
**/node_modules/

# Build output
**/dist/
**/build/

# Vite cache
**/.vite/

# .NET build output
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Environment & secrets (never commit real keys)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local editor / agent config. Skills are the exception: settings.local.json is one
# machine's preferences, but a skill is shared knowledge about how this repo works —
# the same reason HANDOFF and scripts/catalogue/README.md are committed. Ignored, it
# would vanish on a fresh clone and reach nobody.
**/.claude/*
!**/.claude/skills/
**/.vs/

# SPA build output. Vite builds the frontend straight into the API's web root, and
# `dotnet publish` regenerates it (see the BuildSpa target in api-dotnet.csproj), so
# it is generated, never authored. Source of truth is "NVC Claude version/".
# Deploys are Zip Deploy from the publish output, so nothing here needs committing.
api-dotnet/wwwroot/

# Prerendered page snapshots (scripts/prerender.mjs). Same category as wwwroot above:
# generated from the app, never authored, and regenerated as a release step (DEPLOY.md
# §6b) before the Zip Deploy picks them up. Committing them would put ~50 near-identical
# 35 KB HTML files into every content-change diff.
api-dotnet/prerendered/

# Visual Studio publish profile user settings. These hold the App Service deployment
# credential (<EncryptedPassword>) and are per-developer, per-machine — they must never
# be committed. The .pubxml files themselves are shared and stay tracked.
*.pubxml.user

# Per-developer IDE state (last used publish profile, etc). Machine-specific absolute
# paths, so it just churns between machines and has no shared value.
*.csproj.user

# Logs & OS cruft
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The accessibility sweep's scratch output (npm run audit:a11y)
"NVC Claude version/a11y-report.json"
a11y-report.json
